  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/7A3D88">Corollary <span data-tag="7A3D88">2.1.2.9</span>.</a>left fibration!and functor categories Let $p: X \rightarrow S$ be a left-fibration, and let $i: A \rightarrow B$ be any cofibration of simplicial sets. Then the induced map $q: X^{B} \rightarrow X^ A \times _{ S^ A } S^ B$ is a left fibration. If $i$ is left anodyne, then $q$ is a trivial Kan fibration. </p>
